PhotoFramer (`photoframer-7b-q4_k_m.gguf` and `photoframer-7b-mmproj-f16.gguf`)
is MIT, published as PyTorch weights and converted on a development machine
by `scripts/convert-photoframer.sh`. It is not in the download catalogue and
has no catalogue digest. Upstream weights:
https://huggingface.co/zhiyuanyou/Qwen2.5-VL-7B-GRPO-Composition-Score-Class
The converted weight is about 4.4 GB. Public hosting for the converted
GGUF files is not decided yet; scripts/fetch-models.sh skips them unless
VB_PHOTOFRAMER_URL and VB_PHOTOFRAMER_MMPROJ_URL are set.

Every other model downloads from the upstream URL in the table above
(models-manifest.json, scripts/fetch-models.sh). An optional GitHub Release
mirror splits any file over 1.9 GiB (`split -b 1900M -d -a 2`); the script
joins the parts and checks the whole file.

Whisper weights: OpenAI Whisper, MIT, via the whisper.cpp ggml files.
Qwen3-VL weights: Apache-2.0, Qwen.
Depth Anything V2 Small: Apache-2.0. YuNet and PP-HumanSeg: the ONNX files
published in the OpenCV model zoos linked above (MIT and Apache-2.0 as
catalogued). AuraFace v1: Apache-2.0, fal. RTMO-s: Apache-2.0, OpenMMLab,
ONNX export by Xenova. SigLIP 2: Apache-2.0, Google, fp16 ONNX export by
onnx-community. The scene-label table embedded in `vb-onnx` was produced
from that text tower on the development side; the text tower itself is not
shipped.

## Other data and tools

- Map outlines in `vb-geo` are Natural Earth, public domain
  (https://www.naturalearthdata.com/). A map shown in an app published in
  mainland China needs a review number (审图号). These outlines do not have
  one.
- The Flutter application and its engine shell are this project's code under
  the AGPL. Flutter itself is BSD-3-Clause (https://flutter.dev/).
- The Gradle wrapper scripts and `gradle-wrapper.jar` under `app/android`
  are Gradle's, Apache-2.0 (https://gradle.org/).
- Rust crate licenses are enforced by `core/deny.toml`. Copyleft dependencies
  other than this project's own crates are refused.

## Not included

CoTracker3 and MMAudio are CC-BY-NC and are not dependencies.
World Monitor and LosslessCut are not included; the memory map borrows a
look only, and lossless export follows an idea only.
